<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFrameworks>netcoreapp3.1;net6.0;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <AssemblyName>SmbSharp</AssemblyName>
        <RootNamespace>SmbSharp</RootNamespace>
        <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>

        <!-- NuGet Package Configuration -->
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <PackageId>SmbSharp</PackageId>
        <Version>2.0.0-preview.5</Version>
        <Authors>Diego Dancourt</Authors>
        <Company>Diego Dancourt</Company>
        <Product>SmbSharp</Product>
        <Description>A cross-platform .NET library for SMB/CIFS file operations. Supports both Kerberos and username/password authentication. Works on Windows (native UNC) and Linux/macOS (via smbclient).</Description>
        <Copyright>Copyright © Diego Dancourt 2026</Copyright>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/diegodancourt/SmbSharp</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/diegodancourt/SmbSharp</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageTags>smb;cifs;smbclient;file;share;network;kerberos;cross-platform;wsl;macos</PackageTags>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>v2.0.0-preview.5: PREVIEW - Fix session-pool WriteFileAsync failing under WSL: pooled ExecuteAsync did not translate embedded Windows temp-file paths (e.g. "put C:\...\file remote") to their WSL /mnt/&lt;drive&gt;/... equivalents before sending to smbclient, unlike the non-pooled path. v2.0.0-preview.4: PREVIEW - Fix root cause of session pool hang: smbclient never emits its interactive prompt "smb: \&gt; " at all (not just buffered) unless stdin is a TTY. Output buffering fixes alone (stdbuf) could not solve this. Now invokes smbclient through "script -qec" to allocate a real pseudo-terminal, restoring prompt output; verified end-to-end against a live share, including natively inside Linux (WSL) with no wsl.exe relay involved. v2.0.0-preview.3: PREVIEW - Fix session pool still hanging: line-buffering (stdbuf -oL) does not flush smbclient's interactive prompt "smb: \&gt; " because it has no trailing newline. Switched to fully-unbuffered stdbuf -o0 -e0. v2.0.0-preview.2: PREVIEW - Fix persistent session pool hanging indefinitely: smbclient fully buffers stdout when not attached to a TTY, so the interactive prompt/banner could sit unflushed and never reach the reader. Now invokes smbclient via stdbuf -oL -eL to force line-buffered output. v2.0.0-preview.1: PREVIEW - Add persistent session pool support (UseSessionPool option) to avoid re-authenticating (full connect/negotiate/Kerberos handshake) on every smbclient call. Keeps a small pool of persistent, authenticated smbclient sessions per share; transparently recreates and retries once if a session dies mid-operation. v1.1.2: Repackage of v1.1.1 fixes with clean build (previous package contained stale binaries). Fix EnumerateFilesAsync on smbclient path: include files with any attribute (not just Archive), correctly parse filenames containing spaces, return empty list for empty directories instead of throwing, and include hidden dot-files. v1.1.0: Add macOS support (smbclient), WSL smbclient support on Windows (opt-in), and sample console app.</PackageReleaseNotes>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
        <None Include="..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SmbSharp.Tests" />
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="DynamicProxyGenAssembly2" Key="" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="3.1.0" />
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Diagnostics.HealthChecks" Version="3.1.0" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
